  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): マジョラム",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9E%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%A0",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 106376049,
      "text": "マジョラム は、シソ科の多年草。ハーブとして様々な用途に用いられる。和名はマヨラナ。オレガノなど同じ属の他の種と区別するためスイート・マジョラム 、あるいはノッテッド・マジョラム とも呼ばれている。30センチメートル程度の茂みに育ち、赤みがかった枝に、対になった丸く白い葉がつく。初夏に、先端に白い花を多数つける。ハーブのオレガノは同属。マージョラムとも表記される。肉料理の香りづけに使われるハーブとしても知られる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Marjoram",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjoram",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1375540427,
      "text": "Marjoram is a cold-sensitive perennial herb or undershrub with sweet pine and citrus flavours. In some Middle Eastern countries, marjoram is synonymous with oregano, and there the names sweet marjoram and knotted marjoram are used to distinguish it from other plants of the genus Origanum. It is also called pot marjoram, although this name is also used for other cultivated species of Origanum."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Origanum majorana",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origanum_majorana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171581468,
      "text": "Origanum majorana, comúnmente llamada mejorana, mayorana, marjorama o almoraduj, es una hierba vivaz de la familia Lamiaceae, cultivada como condimento por su aroma, parecido al del orégano."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Marjolaine",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjolaine",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 237081329,
      "text": "La marjolaine ou origan des jardins est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Lamiacées. C'est une plante herbacée vivace originaire du bassin méditerranéen et cultivée ailleurs comme plante condimentaire pour ses feuilles aromatiques. C'est une espèce très proche de l'origan commun."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Manjerona",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manjerona",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 64917897,
      "text": "A manjerona é uma erva ou planta perene, com sabores doces a pinho e citrino."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Marjoram",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjoram",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29302027,
      "text": "Marjoram merupakan sejenis tanaman yang biasanya dibuat untuk permen. Juga biasanya disebut Sweet Marjoram atau Knotted Marjoram dan Majorana hortensis. Tanaman ini merupakan rempah-rempah yang populer, sehingga tidak hanya dibiakkan di negara-negara Mediterania, tetapi juga di negara-negara Asia."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Marjoram § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjoram#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1375540427,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Considered a tender perennial (USDA Zones 7–9), marjoram can sometimes prove hardy even in zone 5. Under proper conditions it spreads prolifically, and so is usually grown in pots to prevent it from taking over a garden.\nMarjoram is cultivated for its aromatic leaves, either green or dry, for culinary purposes; the tops are cut as the plants begin to flower and are dried slowly in the shade. It is often used in herb combinations such as herbes de Provence and za'atar. The flowering leaves and tops of marjoram are steam-distilled to produce an essential oil that is yellowish (darkening to brown as it ages). It has many chemical components, some of which are borneol, camphor, and pinene.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Marjolaine § Culture",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjolaine#Culture",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 237081329,
        "heading": "Culture",
        "text": "C'est une vivace cultivée comme une annuelle. Elle peut être multipliée par éclats de touffe et par semis. Elle a besoin d'une exposition ensoleillée et ne supporte pas l'humidité combinée au froid. Elle supporte légèrement le gel puisque sa zone de rusticité se situe entre 6 et 9. Floraison juillet/août.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
